# What the image is built from is smaller than it looks: the crate source, the `pokered`
# submodule's *source*, and the `web/` npm project. Everything else is either regenerated inside
# the image or would make the context enormous — `target/` alone is 11 GB.

target/
**/node_modules/
**/.git
.git/
.gitignore
.gitmodules
runs/
docs/
tools/
.github/
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml

# Runtime files of a desktop run; the container never loads either.
pokemon-red.sav
pokemon-red.bin

# ⚠️ Built by stage 2 (`pnpm run build`), never taken from the host — a `dist/` from a different
# checkout would be baked into the binary by `rust-embed` and nothing would say so.
web/dist/

# ⚠️ Built by stage 1, for the same reason and one more: these are *host* artifacts. A stale
# `pokered.gbc`, or an x86-64 `tools/gfx` in an arm64 build, would either ship silently or fail
# somewhere far from the cause. None of them is tracked in the submodule — every one is generated
# by `make` — so excluding the lot loses nothing.
#
# ⚠️ The `**` is load-bearing: `pokered/*.o` alone leaves `pokered/gfx/pics_red.o` in the context,
# and a host object file built by a *newer* rgbds stops the build dead inside the container
# ("Unsupported object file ... expected revision 12, got 13"). Found exactly that way.
pokered/**/*.o
pokered/**/*.gbc
pokered/**/*.sym
pokered/**/*.map
pokered/**/*.patch
pokered/**/*.1bpp
pokered/**/*.2bpp
pokered/**/*.pic
pokered/tools/gfx
pokered/tools/make_patch
pokered/tools/pkmncompress
pokered/tools/scan_includes
